; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Permutation Beads
; CATEGORY: Algorithms
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     permutations, recursion, lists, counting
; SUMMARY:  Generates every ordering of four colored beads with a short recursive procedure and lays all 24 strings out on the screen.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   PERMS takes a list and outputs a list of every way to order it.
;   Four colors give 4 x 3 x 2 x 1 = 24 orderings. Each one is drawn as
;   a string of beads, in a grid of 6 columns and 4 rows. Each row of
;   six strings shares the same first bead, while the other three beads
;   are shuffled into all their six orders behind it.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change :beads to three colors (6 strings) or keep four.
;   Five colors make 120 strings, which is too many to draw at this size.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * the recursive idea: pick a first item, then permute the rest
;   * MAP and MAP.SE to build lists of lists
;   * REMOVE to take one item out of a list
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Print PERMS [a b c] and check the six answers by hand.
;   * Use PERMS on a list of letters such as [t e a] and join each
;     answer with (APPLY "WORD ?) to see every jumbled spelling.
; ============================================================

make "beads [red yellow cyan magenta]

; Every ordering of a list. For each item x: take x out, find every
; ordering of what is left, and stick x on the front of each one.
; MAP.SE joins the little lists of answers into one big list.
to perms :items
  if emptyp butfirst :items [output (list :items)]
  output map.se [[x] map [[rest] fput :x :rest] perms remove :x :items] :items
end

; One string of beads, starting at x y and going right.
to bead.string :x :y :colors
  setpencolor "#808890 setpensize 2
  penup setxy :x :y pendown setxy :x + 28 * ((count :colors) - 1) :y
  setpensize 22
  foreach :colors [
    setpencolor ?
    dot (list :x + 28 * (# - 1) :y)
  ]
  setpensize 1
end

to lay.out :all
  localmake "k 0
  foreach :all [
    localmake "col remainder :k 6
    localmake "row int :k / 6
    bead.string -340 + :col * 125 180 - :row * 110 ?
    make "k :k + 1
    wait 10
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground "#1a1a22
make "all perms :beads
lay.out :all
print (sentence count :all [different orderings of] count :beads [beads.])
print [The first three orderings are:]
repeat 3 [show item repcount :all]
